Subject: [PATCH 20/22] fix(capture): preserve ancestry for reasoning Responses
 (#3301)

## What does this PR do?

Fix external token-capture ancestry by recording the final API response
representation, after Chat, Responses, or Anthropic Messages conversion
and JSON serialization succeed.

The original reasoning continuation bug reproduces on main at
`9506eb87c99ffa0f736b05f76b8f20dca8fb479b`: capture fingerprints an
internal Chat assistant message with wrapped reasoning, while the
Responses client echoes separate reasoning and answer items. Generation
returns HTTP 200, but capture is poisoned with `unresolved_parent`.

Following [Ananth's
review](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Gym/pull/3301#pullrequestreview-5176149311),
this revision replaces the initial URL-selected conversion workaround
with the post-conversion design from [his final commit in
#3050](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Gym/commit/4c67a8677ee79e38bd8177a13e22acfb51a2e89b):

- Retain worker commit coordinates privately in the existing
request-scoped capture context; immediately strip transport fields from
the internal response.
- Finalize once at the outer Chat, Responses, or Messages dispatch
boundary, after conversion and JSON serialization.
- Normalize served Anthropic thinking blocks into standalone reasoning
items when constructing capture output items.
- Preserve the existing worker-acknowledgement validation, token-free
ledger, response-ID association, and poison-and-serve capture behavior.

This also fixes the reviewer's refusal example: Responses refusal
content becomes ordinary text in Messages, so fingerprinting the
intermediate Responses representation is wrong. Conversion/serialization
failures now leave no successful lineage row; the existing middleware
marks the admitted call uncommitted. Finalization before HTTP send is
not a guarantee of client receipt.

No fingerprint algorithm, admission rules, token-staging protocol,
dependencies, lockfiles, or agent implementations change. Only the
finalization portion of #3050 is adapted, not its inherited capture
infrastructure. Refusal-only direct Chat ambiguity under the existing
fingerprint rules is outside this change; the original direct Chat
reasoning/plain-text controls remain covered.

## Validation

- Retained the original 24 three-turn HTTP cases: Responses, Chat
Completions, and Messages; plain answers and three reasoning
representations; with and without tool calls.
- Added four refusal continuation cases for Responses and Messages, with
and without tool calls.
- Added five failure cases: Responses/Messages conversion and JSON
serialization on all three APIs. Worker staging must already have
succeeded, no lineage commit may occur, and capture must be marked
uncommitted.
- Continuation cases check exact parent IDs and cumulative prefix
lengths, one ledger commit per call, the served response ID, token-light
output, and rejection of subsequently altered history.
- Before the revision, the Messages refusal and post-staging
conversion-failure regressions failed as reported. The original
reasoning regressions also remain regression-tested against the original
main baseline (12 failed, 12 passed before the original fix).
- After the revision: **811 passed** across vLLM model tests,
Responses/base-model/Anthropic converters, and token-capture suites. The
focused integration file has **35 passing tests**.
- `pre-commit run --all-files` passes.

These tests use the real HTTP dispatch, middleware, converters, worker
capture helper, file ledger, and parent admission. Generation and
staging storage are CPU doubles; no live vLLM/GPU validation of this
revision is claimed.

```bash
python -m pytest responses_api_models/vllm_model/tests/test_token_capture_integration.py
```

